Subject: [PATCH] fix(test): avoid pytest logger registry capture race (#234)

* fix(test): avoid pytest logger registry capture race

* fix(kanban): keep placement attribution out of chat routing [daveey]

* fix(kanban): exclude placement placeholders from live pollers [daveey]

* fix(kanban): derive scope-heartbeat freshness from the owner's published collector period [daveey]

Remote-terminal release, origin-ledger owner liveness and wait probes each trusted an owner's
task_scopes[].observed_at for a fixed window (450 s, 450 s, 600 s). On the loaded hub the gap between
clean scope reads reached ~440 s (default-board reads timing out at 180 s), so closed remote cards
flapped "never released" in session-idle-check, both directions.

New hermes_cli/kanban_scope_heartbeat.py is the one rule: window = clamp(2.5 x
scope_heartbeat_period_s, 450, 1800), where the owner's hermes-hub collector publishes the period in
gateway/info. An owner that publishes none keeps the 450 s floor. Tests pin window >= 2.5 x period
and exercise each reader (release, projection horizon, ledger, wait probe).

* test(update): publish stand-in backend port atomically [daveey] (#229)

* fix(kanban): admit board reads per board so a cold board cannot queue the others [daveey]

Mac 16:30 cold start (loop-watch, 9 records): GET /api/plugins/kanban/board
took 6-20 s. Every board read waited at web_read_coalescing.py:51 on the one
asyncio.Semaphore(1) shared by all of _read_board, so a cheap read of one board
queued behind a cold read of another (the runners board hit the Desktop's 6 s
timeout). Hub repro with the real data: runners read admit_wait 6.1 s, run 0.4 s.

coalesced_read gains admission_key/max_concurrent: one in-flight read per
group, at most N groups at once. _read_board groups by board, N=4, so a burst
still holds a bounded number of AnyIO workers; /api/profiles keeps one slot.

* fix(test): avoid pytest logger registry capture race
